{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is an unattended coordinator loop. It repeatedly launches me as an INDEPENDENT adjudicator for lanes of the ai-template kit repo (`C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-NNN`). Each turn is one of these kinds:\n   - **Dispute sittings:** rule each finding FIX, SUCCESSOR, DISMISS (out-of-scope, refuted or not-worth-cost) or ESCALATE, under PROCESS.md §6 \"Review threat model\". A convergence-class finding (fail-open, data loss, or a Done-when gap) is never SUCCESSOR.\n   - **Amendment sittings:** CLARITY or MEANING. Mark `[MEANING+BLESS]` for a released-rung row I would bless. A held rung (SN tier) is recommended to the owner only.\n   - **First-approval sittings:** APPROVE or RETURN.\n   - **Done-when sittings:** CLARITY, BLESSED or SUCCESSOR, with the digest copied verbatim.\n   - **Act turns:** a reattest snapshot, then Status flips plus an approves snapshot, each its own commit.\n\n   Rules for every verdict:\n   - ONE verdict file per sitting, with `## <kind>` headings and the machine lines, ending in `SITTING: JUDGED kinds=...`.\n   - Commit once, with `WI: WI-NNN` plus the current `Loop-Session:` trailer in the same final trailer block, then `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n   - Decomposition rounds (an SR awaiting first approval, or an amended SN) need one `- HAT <NAME> -> ... -> ...` line per listed hat, once per sitting, under the last section.\n\n   Constraints, verbatim in spirit:\n   - \"Do not edit the code, the review, the findings file or any registry\"; \"Do NOT edit any registry CELL either way\".\n   - Act turns: \"You may not write or edit anything under `docs/reviews/`, edit any registry cell but a listed row's `Status`, or approve or re-attest a row that is not listed\"; \"If the snapshot REFUSES, naming a row that is not listed ... Stop there: commit nothing further, and report the refusal.\"\n   - `OWNER_SCRATCHPAD.md` is owner-only: never read, cite, or act on it.\n   - \"Fail toward RETURN\" / \"Fail toward MEANING\"; \"Judge the CELLS BELOW and nothing else\"; \"an amendment's author is not a witness to their own intent\".\n   - KEEP THE QUOTES on `--approves` values.\n\n   The current Loop-Session trailer is `Loop-Session: 20261031T174835Z-e602ab`. Earlier ones were 20261021T045653Z-213020, 20261024T053017Z-23122f and 20261025T055732Z-64b2b6.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - The SN→SR→LLR→TC spine and its registries:\n     - `docs/requirements/{system-requirements,low-level-requirements,stakeholder-needs}.toml` (tables `requirement`, `design`, `need`);\n     - `docs/test/test-cases.toml` (table `test`);\n     - the snapshot `docs/archive/last_approved/`, with its `acts.toml` and README stamp.\n   - Released vs held rungs: SN is held for the owner; LLR, SR and TC are released.\n   - Naming rule: no code names in row text, and an amendment adds no forbidden name. I applied it to returns in WI-851 (LLR-249, TC-243, TC-278) and WI-976 (LLR-273): drop the module qualifier and keep the approved symbol verbatim.\n   - An acceptance criterion cannot mint obligations its Requirement lacks (WI-850 SR-224). One `shall` per SR; don't state a second obligation as a fact outside the `shall`.\n   - Perspective records (`*.perspectives.toml`, `hats.py record --check --strict`) existed until WI-976 retired them. Now the decomposition brief carries hat questions, and the verdict names each hat's outcome.\n   - Stopping boundary: decomposition-round verdicts must state, per chain, why splitting stops (SR-186 / TC-211). I saved a memory about this.\n   - The held-rung lane rule (SR-208, WI-851): a held approval lands from a lane only as a CLARITY re-attestation bound to its digest.\n   - The parent-first rule (WI-850). Snapshot refresh refusal: a drifted, unblessed row in a copied registry blocks that registry's act.\n   - Removals are briefed and re-attested via `--reattests` (WI-976 LLR-297, TC-312).\n   - Done-when blessing digest grammar: the `DONE-WHEN:` machine line with `changes=` and `digest=` (checked; no line-count validation).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Verdict files written and committed:**\n     - wi-960: 006 (b9b51182b)\n     - wi-961: 002 (26f4c6007), 007 (932d2f055), 008 (afb72e490), 009 (4490d2347)\n     - wi-850: 001 (a2ebc15ff), 002 (dbf2e5252), 003 (243232c63), 006 (bf7536fff)\n     - wi-851: 003 (5768ae162), 004 (43867cea7)\n     - wi-856: 003 (1ee762253)\n     - wi-878: 003 (6ef0a2385)\n     - wi-976: 004 (4020f97a5), 010 (dc7461730), 011 (28eb00696), 012 (bee5b9a28), 015 (ff639cbe5), 016 (6ec31d938), 021 (a9be83f29), 024 (ca31fd75e)\n     - wi-966: 003 (31a03623a), 006 (b540e3ac5), 007 (696081ee3)\n   - **Act commits:**\n     - wi-960: c7cbab713, 4adbbb131\n     - wi-961: 63d872547\n     - wi-850: cd5292585, 2b14b2cc6\n     - wi-851: 806d7b1c4, 818d0a7f0\n     - wi-856: 652c0e68e\n     - wi-878: e812d9b04\n     - wi-976: 9aa5bd28b, 9ea92b59e\n     - wi-966: 7cefc0507\n   - **Memory created:**\n     - `C:\\Users\\Peter\\AppData\\Roaming\\project-trajectory\\accounts\\ADJUDICATOR\\projects\\C--Projects-ai-template\\memory\\stopping-boundary-in-verdicts.md` (feedback type) and its `MEMORY.md` index line.\n   - **The byte-preserving flip script used in act turns** (run with the venv python `-I`, from `$env:TEMP\\flipNNN.py`):\n     ```python\n     import re\n     plan = {\"docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml\": [\"LLR-xxx\"], \"docs/test/test-cases.toml\": [\"TC-yyy\"]}\n     for path, ids in plan.items():\n         lines = open(path,\"rb\").read().split(b\"\\n\")\n         for rid in ids:\n             hdr=[i for i,l in enumerate(lines) if re.match(rb\"^\\[[a-z_]+\\.\"+rid.encode()+rb\"\\]\\s*$\", l)]\n             assert len(hdr)==1, (rid, hdr)\n             i=hdr[0]+1\n             while i<len(lines) and not lines[i].startswith(b\"[\") and not re.match(rb'^status = \"', lines[i]): i+=1\n             assert lines[i].rstrip(b\"\\r\")==b'status = \"Drafted\"', (rid, lines[i])\n             cr=b\"\\r\" if lines[i].endswith(b\"\\r\") else b\"\"\n             lines[i]=b'status = \"Approved\"'+cr\n         open(path,\"wb\").write(b\"\\n\".join(lines))\n     print(\"ok\")\n     ```\n   - **Snapshot commands, run in PowerShell:**\n     ```\n     & \"C:\\Projects\\ai-template\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe\" project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py snapshot --reattests A,B\n     ```\n     or `... --approves \"reg=WI-NNN;reg=WI-NNN\"`, keeping the quotes.\n   - **Commit pattern (PowerShell here-string):**\n     ```\n     git add <file>\n     git commit -q -m @'\n     WI-NNN: <subject>\n\n     WI: WI-NNN\n     Loop-Session: 20261031T174835Z-e602ab\n     Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n     '@ *> $env:TEMP\\cNNN.txt\n     ```\n   - **WI-966 code reproduced for dispute 006:** `project-trajectory/scripts/bootstrap.py`.\n     - `set_process_key` (~line 939) and `_locate_process_key` were line-shape based.\n     - `apply_privacy_check` ignored the `missing` result, and main printed `privacy-check: true` at line 2715.\n     - `migrate_legacy_config` appended a duplicate `[policies]` header, or rewrote a line inside a multi-line string, and deleted the legacy file.\n     - The fix at b724c341c raises `PolicyWriteRefused` (verified at sitting 007).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Missing `scripts/intake.py`:** it doesn't exist at the repo root. Use `project-trajectory/scripts/intake.py`.\n   - **PATH python lacks tomllib:** use the venv python.\n   - **WI-976 act on sitting 012 refused:** it named the removed LLR-297 and TC-312, which weren't listed. I stopped and committed nothing, as instructed. The lane later fixed the composer to brief removals, and sitting 015/016 ruled them.\n   - **Wrong word